  "title": "Pohela Boishakh",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**পহেলা বৈশাখ**, the first day of the month of Boishakh, is the Bengali New Year. In Bangladesh it falls on **14 April**, and people of every religion celebrate it together. Greet everyone with **শুভ নববর্ষ!** 'Happy New Year!'\n\nTraditions:\n\n- red and white clothes (often a white sari with a red border)\n- **আলপনা** patterns painted on floors and streets\n- a **মেলা** (fair) with crafts, toys and snacks\n- in Dhaka, songs at sunrise and a big, colourful street procession\n- **পান্তা ভাত** (rice soaked overnight in water) with fried ইলিশ\n- shopkeepers open a new account book (*halkhata*) and offer sweets\n\n**শুভ** + occasion is a common pattern: **শুভ নববর্ষ**, and later *shubho jonmodin* 'happy birthday'. (**শুভ সকাল** 'good morning' is mostly for messages.)\n\n**মেলা** 'fair' → **মেলায়** 'to / at the fair': **তুমি কি মেলায় যাবে?** 'Will you go to the fair?'\n\n**Kolkata:** **পয়লা বৈশাখ** (*poyla boishakh*), on 14 or 15 April.",
